<item>
            <title>[KYLIN-5525] When the excluded column is enabled and the query hits multiple identical models at the same time, the query may push down</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KYLIN-5525</link>
                <project id="12316121" key="KYLIN">Kylin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When there is only a table index, union all and its two subqueries can respond quickly. When the aggregate index is added, the subquery can hit the model, but the union all statement is pushdown&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#24403;&#21482;&#26377;&#26126;&#32454;&#32034;&#24341;&#26102;&#65292;union all&#21450;&#20854;&#20004;&#20010;&#23376;&#26597;&#35810;&#37117;&#33021;&#24456;&#24555;&#21709;&#24212;&#65292;&#24403;&#22686;&#21152;&#20102;&#32858;&#21512;&#32034;&#24341;&#21518;&#65292;&#23376;&#26597;&#35810;&#21487;&#20197;&#20987;&#20013;&#27169;&#22411;&#65292;&#20294;&#26159;union all&#35821;&#21477;&#36208;&#20102;&#19979;&#21387;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13533939">KYLIN-5525</key>
            <summary>When the excluded column is enabled and the query hits multiple identical models at the same time, the query may push down</summary>
